.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt POUDRIERE-HOOKS 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm poudriere-hooks
.Nd hook scripts and plugins run by poudriere
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /usr/local/etc/poudriere.d/hooks/ Ns Ar hook Ns Pa .sh
.Pp
.Pa /usr/local/etc/poudriere.d/hooks/plugins/ Ns Ar plugin Ns Pa / Ns Ar hook Ns Pa .sh
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr poudriere 8
runs hook scripts at fixed points of its work, for example when a
.Cm bulk
run starts or ends, when a builder starts, or when the build of a
package succeeds or fails.
A hook script can send a notification, publish a repository, record
statistics, or prepare a builder.
.Pp
Each point has a
.Ar hook
name and an
.Ar event
name.
The hook name selects the file,
.Ar hook Ns Pa .sh ;
the event is passed to the script as its first argument.
One script therefore handles all events of its hook and has to check
the first argument.
A hook without a script file is silently skipped.
.Ss Hook files and plugins
For each hook
.Xr poudriere 8
first runs
.Pa hooks/ Ns Ar hook Ns Pa .sh
and then
.Pa hooks/plugins/ Ns Ar plugin Ns Pa / Ns Ar hook Ns Pa .sh
for every plugin directory, in alphabetical order.
A plugin is a directory that holds the hook scripts of one add-on, so
that several add-ons can use the same hook without sharing a file.
.Pp
A plugin directory may also contain a file
.Pa make.conf .
It is appended to the
.Pa make.conf
of the jail after the files described in
.Xr poudriere 8 .
.Ss How a hook is run
.Bl -bullet
.It
The script is run with
.Pa /bin/sh .
The interpreter line and the execute permission of the file are ignored.
.It
It is called as
.Ar hook Ns Pa .sh
.Ar event
.Op Ar argument ...
.It
It runs on the host, as the user running
.Xr poudriere 8 ,
not inside a jail.
.It
The working directory is
.Pa /tmp
and standard input is
.Pa /dev/null .
.It
If the script exits with a non-zero status,
.Xr poudriere 8
stops with an error.
A script that must never interrupt a build has to end with
.Ql exit 0 .
.It
.Xr poudriere 8
waits for the script.
A slow
.Ql pkgbuild
or
.Ql builder
hook slows down the whole build.
.El
.Sh HOOKS
The arguments listed here follow the event name.
.Ss bulk
Run by
.Xr poudriere-bulk 8
only.
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm start
The run starts, before the jail is started.
.It Cm done Ar built failed ignored skipped fetched
The run has finished.
The arguments are the numbers of built, failed, ignored, skipped and
fetched packages.
.It Cm crashed
The run ended abnormally, for example after an internal error or a
signal.
.El
.Ss pkgbuild
Run once for each package of the queue.
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm success Ar origin pkgname
The package was built.
.It Cm failed Ar origin pkgname phase logfile
The build failed in
.Ar phase ,
for example
.Ql build
or
.Ql stage .
.Ar logfile
is the log of the failed build.
.It Cm ignored Ar origin pkgname reason
The port is marked
.Dv IGNORE ,
.Dv BROKEN
or similar.
.Ar reason
is the text given by the port.
.It Cm skipped Ar origin pkgname dependency
The port was not built because the port
.Ar dependency
failed or was ignored.
Not run for a dry run
.Pq Fl n .
.El
.Ss jail
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm start
The master jail has been started.
.It Cm stop
The master jail is about to be stopped.
.It Cm mount Ar mountpoint
The file systems of a jail have been mounted under
.Ar mountpoint .
.It Cm pkgbase Ar repository
.Xr poudriere-jail 8
has created the base system packages of a jail in the directory
.Ar repository .
.El
.Ss builder
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm start Ar id mountpoint
Builder
.Ar id
has been created; its root directory is
.Ar mountpoint .
.It Cm stop Ar id mountpoint
Builder
.Ar id
is about to be stopped.
.El
.Ss pkgrepo
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm sign Ar packages key from_host meta_file
Run just before
.Xr pkg-repo 8 .
The arguments are the package directory and the values of
.Va PKG_REPO_SIGNING_KEY ,
.Va PKG_REPO_FROM_HOST
and
.Va PKG_REPO_META_FILE .
.It Cm publish Ar packages
The repository in
.Ar packages
is complete and has been committed.
After a build with failures it is run only if
.Va COMMIT_PACKAGES_ON_FAILURE
allows the commit.
.El
.Ss pkgclean
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm done Ar deleted build_repo force_build_repo
.Xr poudriere-pkgclean 8
has finished.
.Ar deleted
is 1 if packages were deleted and 0 otherwise.
.Ar build_repo
is 0 if rebuilding the repository was disabled with
.Fl N
and 1 otherwise.
.Ar force_build_repo
is 1 if a rebuild was forced with
.Fl u .
.El
.Ss ports_update
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm done
.Cm poudriere ports -u
has updated a ports tree.
.El
.Ss foreachport
.Bl -tag -width "crashed"
.It Cm start , Cm stop
Run before and after the
.Cm foreachport
command processes the ports.
.El
.Ss Hooks around the steps of a build
These hooks have the events
.Cm start
and
.Cm stop
and no arguments.
They are mostly useful to measure or debug
.Xr poudriere 8
itself.
.Bl -tag -width "gather_port_vars"
.It Cm gather_port_vars
Reading the metadata of the ports.
.It Cm generate_queue
Creating the build queue.
.It Cm compute_deps
Calculating the dependencies.
.It Cm delete_old_pkgs
Checking which existing packages are out of date.
.It Cm start_builders
Creating the builders.
.It Cm build_queue
Building the packages of the queue.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Every hook gets these variables.
A variable is empty if it has no meaning at that point; for example
.Ev MY_BUILDER_ID
is only set in hooks run by a builder.
.Bl -tag -width "POUDRIERE_BUILD_TYPE"
.It Ev BUILDNAME
Name of the build, see
.Va BUILDNAME_FORMAT
in
.Pa poudriere.conf .
.It Ev BUILD_URL
Web address of the build, if
.Va URL_BASE
is set.
.It Ev JAILNAME
Name of the jail.
.It Ev LOG
Log directory of the build.
.It Ev LOG_URL
Web address of the logs, if
.Va URL_BASE
is set.
.It Ev MASTERMNT
Root directory of the master jail, from which the builders are cloned.
.It Ev MASTERNAME
Name of the master jail:
.Ar jail Ns - Ns Ar tree ,
followed by
.No - Ns Ar set
if a set is used.
.It Ev MY_BUILDER_ID
Id of the builder that runs the hook.
.It Ev MY_JOBID
Old name of
.Ev MY_BUILDER_ID ;
deprecated.
.It Ev PACKAGES
Package directory of this build.
With
.Va ATOMIC_PACKAGE_REPOSITORY
it is a subdirectory of
.Ev PACKAGES_ROOT .
.It Ev PACKAGES_ROOT
Top-level package directory.
.It Ev POUDRIERED
The
.Pa poudriere.d
directory.
.It Ev POUDRIERE_BUILD_TYPE
Always
.Ql bulk ,
also for
.Cm testport .
.It Ev POUDRIERE_DATA
The data directory, by default
.Pa /usr/local/poudriere/data .
.It Ev PTNAME
Name of the ports tree.
.It Ev SETNAME
Name of the set
.Pq Fl z ,
or empty.
.It Ev VERBOSE
Number of
.Fl v
flags given, 0 or more.
.El
.Pp
Settings of
.Pa poudriere.conf
are not passed to hooks.
To pass one, export it there:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
export MY_HOOK_VALUE=someval
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "hooks/plugins/plugin/make.conf" -compact
.It Pa hooks/ Ns Ar hook Ns Pa .sh
Hook script.
.It Pa hooks/plugins/ Ns Ar plugin Ns Pa / Ns Ar hook Ns Pa .sh
Hook script of a plugin.
.It Pa hooks/plugins/ Ns Ar plugin Ns Pa /make.conf
Additions of a plugin to
.Pa make.conf .
.El
.Pp
All paths are relative to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/poudriere.d .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr poudriere 8 ,
.Xr poudriere-bulk 8 ,
.Xr poudriere-jail 8 ,
.Xr poudriere-pkgclean 8 ,
.Xr poudriere-ports 8 ,
.Xr poudriere-repo 8 ,
.Xr poudriere-testport 8
.Sh CAVEATS
.Xr poudriere-testport 8
does not run the
.Ql bulk
hook.
It runs the
.Ql jail ,
.Ql builder
and build step hooks, and the
.Ql pkgbuild
hook for the dependencies it builds.
.Pp
Hooks are run synchronously and a failing hook stops
.Xr poudriere 8 ,
so a hook should be short and should handle its own errors.
